<!-- BEGIN baseline:commit-attribution v0.1.0 -->
## Portable Agent Baseline: Commit Attribution

- Do not add a `Co-Authored-By: Claude ...` trailer, any other `Co-Authored-By:` line naming an AI, or equivalent co-author metadata to commit messages.
- Do not append "Generated with Claude Code", "Made with <AI>", or similar tool-advertising footers to commits.
- When it is useful to record that a change was AI-assisted, note it in one short prose line in the commit body (e.g. "Assisted by Claude.") rather than a structured co-author trailer.
- Keep the commit subject and body focused on the change itself; attribution is never the headline and never more than a brief note.
- This governs attribution only. Still write descriptive messages, stage explicit paths, and review the staged diff before committing.

Apply this baseline before ordinary commit habits, but never use it to override explicit user instructions, safety rules, privacy boundaries, or stricter repo-local instructions (including a repo convention or user request that explicitly asks for a co-author trailer).
<!-- END baseline:commit-attribution -->
